FIXES                                              risk
  1  Limits for shop-app-1                         medium
  2  Limits for backup.service                     medium
  3  Early out-of-memory protection, systemd-oomd  medium
  4  Heap caps for shop-app-1, after a restart     medium to high
  Preview one with snugbox fit --dry-run 2. Apply it with sudo snugbox fit 2.
  Limits from under 7 days of data are early estimates; snugbox fit asks before using them.
  Note: shop-db-1 is PostgreSQL and holds 628 MiB, 128 MiB of it shared memory, which is mostly shared_buffers. On Vultr vc2-2c-4gb, shared_buffers plus max_connections times work_mem should stay under 1,533 MiB, since one query can use work_mem several times over. PostgreSQL's documentation suggests a quarter of RAM for shared_buffers on a server of its own.

